    {
      "id": "a1ki37a",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "FINAL REVISION POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fk9oecn",
      "content": "1. Physical change does not form a new substance; chemical change forms a new substance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "d8ifmht",
      "content": "2. Indicators of chemical reaction: colour change, gas evolution, temperature change, precipitate formation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x1vdu9r",
      "content": "3. Law of Conservation of Mass: Mass can neither be created nor destroyed."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u163ngl",
      "content": "4. Balanced equation must have equal number of atoms on both sides."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eztqjm4",
      "content": "5. Combination reaction: Two or more reactants form a single product."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0euvv73",
      "content": "6. Decomposition reaction: One compound breaks into simpler substances."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "cv5bu49",
      "content": "7. Displacement reaction occurs according to reactivity series."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oi5hgl5",
      "content": "8. Double displacement involves exchange of ions."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a5r2dl9",
      "content": "9. Neutralisation: Acid + Base → Salt + Water."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u8qvhng",
      "content": "10. Oxidation = Addition of oxygen / Loss of hydrogen / Loss of electrons."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "myjc0ps",
      "content": "11. Reduction = Removal of oxygen / Gain of hydrogen / Gain of electrons."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}